# Supabase (existing)
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Combo Locks allowlist — UI / route gate only (RLS still scopes combo_* rows).
# Comma-separated Google emails and/or Supabase auth uids.
# Kevin's Google account (kev120909@gmail.com) is always included, even if this
# var is empty. Set this in Vercel so testers can see Combo Locks without a code change.
#
# Example:
# VITE_COMBO_LOCKS_ALLOWLIST=kev120909@gmail.com,another@gmail.com,00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
VITE_COMBO_LOCKS_ALLOWLIST=

# Underdog Predict phone prices (odds.prediction). Server-only. Never VITE_.
# Prices come from GET /v1/lobbies/content/match_grouped_lines, not the
# lobby scaffold (sections only, no americans) and not Betstamp book 196.
# These defaults are also in lib/underdog-lobby.js. Set the same values in
# Vercel (Production + Preview + Development). A failed fetch omits the line.
#
# product_experience_id 018e1234-5678-9abc-def0-123456789009 is the phone
# experience (Giants +245 / Rams -313, verified 2026-09-21). Do not replace
# it with b34dfd93-d0e8-4da3-8bf4-45c15c548dec — that id returns sticker +252.
# Headers sent: accept: application/json, client-type: web,
# client-version: 20260918170103.
# UNDERDOG_STATE_CONFIG_ID=f8996742-f10c-4d32-955a-dcbcaa5dc5c0
# UNDERDOG_PRODUCT_EXPERIENCE_ID=018e1234-5678-9abc-def0-123456789009
# UNDERDOG_CLIENT_VERSION=20260918170103
# UNDERDOG_PRODUCT=fantasy
# UNDERDOG_API_BASE=https://api.underdogfantasy.com

# Underdog Predict column gate — New Odds Board + Promo.
# Gate is the signed-in Google/Supabase email (case-insensitive), same pattern as
# Combo Locks. Kevin (kev120909@gmail.com) and Kenneth (kmguido97@gmail.com) are
# always included in code. Add more emails or auth uids here without a code
# change. If you rely on the env-only path, include Kenneth:
# VITE_UNDERDOG_PREDICT_ALLOWLIST=kev120909@gmail.com,kmguido97@gmail.com
# UNDERDOG_PREDICT_ALLOWLIST is also read.
#
# /api/betstamp-markets is anon (no JWT). Promo and the New Odds Board do
# not request book 196. Underdog cells come from /api/underdog-predict
# (odds.prediction). 196 stays on the server allowlist so an explicit
# ?book_ids=196 still parses; the UI will not paint it. Default / omitted
# book_ids omit 196.
#
# Example:
# VITE_UNDERDOG_PREDICT_ALLOWLIST=kev120909@gmail.com,kmguido97@gmail.com
VITE_UNDERDOG_PREDICT_ALLOWLIST=

# Betstamp Pro (server-only). Promo still calls /api/betstamp-markets.
# New Odds Board does not. It loads from Polymarket, Kalshi, and Underdog
# with this key unset or invalid. Never prefix with VITE_ — remaining
# callers talk to /api/betstamp-markets and /api/betstamp-stream, which
# attach X-API-KEY on the server.
# BETSTAMP_API_KEY=

# Optional — send BetMGM (Betstamp book id 400) on /markets and SSE.
# Default is off: the trial key 403s the entire markets request when 400 is
# in book_ids, which emptied New Odds Board LIVE after #187. BetMGM stays
# in the UI catalog (empty cells) until the plan is entitled. Then set:
# BETSTAMP_INCLUDE_BETMGM=1

# Optional — hours ahead of now for Betstamp /fixtures and /markets (default 240).
# Without this, those endpoints only return roughly ±24h, which drops next-week
# NFL/NCAAF slates. Override per request with ?timedelta=.
# BETSTAMP_TIMEDELTA=

# Optional — New Odds Board LIVE presence-reconcile interval (ms). Client-only.
# Default is 10000 (src/betstampLive.js BETSTAMP_LIVE_RECONCILE_MS). Snapshot
# listing is availability truth vs SSE silence. Clamp is 10000–60000.
# VITE_BETSTAMP_LIVE_RECONCILE_MS=

# Optional — how long a live quote can be missing from REST before OFF (ms).
# Clock is last-confirmed / last-seen, not Betstamp updated_at. Default 25000.
# Clamp is 10000–60000 (same resolver as the reconcile interval).
# VITE_BETSTAMP_RECONCILE_CLEAR_GRACE_MS=

# Optional kill switch for Polymarket + Kalshi on New Odds Board.
# Unset is on (pregame and LIVE). Set VITE_FIRST_PARTY_PM_LIVE=0 to hide
# those two columns' feeds. Underdog phone stays. Do not invent API keys.
# VITE_FIRST_PARTY_PM_LIVE=

# Optional — Promo rest-of-book (display only). Kalshi + Polymarket are public/keyless.
# ProphetX / Novig stay top-of-book (Odds API bet_limit) until these are set in Vercel.
# PROPHETX_API_KEY=
# PROPHETX_ACCESS_KEY=
# PROPHETX_SECRET_KEY=
# PROPHETX_API_BASE=https://cash.api.prophetx.co/partner
# NOVIG_CLIENT_ID=
# NOVIG_CLIENT_SECRET=
# NOVIG_API_BASE=https://api.novig.us

# Combo Locks Probe (POST /api/combo-probe) — RSA-PSS, same names as Railway combo-worker.
# kalshi-games.js stays keyless. Probe creates a real RFQ at the lock cap, waits ~4s,
# returns best maker NO bid, then DELETE the RFQ. It never accept/confirms a quote.
# Add these in the Vercel project env (Production + Preview + Development). Do not
# prefix with VITE_ — they are server-only secrets. Do not invent keys here.
#
# KALSHI_KEY_ID=
# Kalshi_combo_key=
# # or, if the worker key is stored under the generic name:
# # KALSHI_PRIVATE_KEY=
#
# Probe owner-gate uses the signed-in Supabase JWT (Authorization: Bearer).
# Server verifies with:
#   SUPABASE_URL  (or VITE_SUPABASE_URL)
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  (or VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY)
# Same Combo Locks allowlist as the UI (Kevin + VITE_COMBO_LOCKS_ALLOWLIST).

# Live Trading Desk (GET/POST /api/live-trading-desk) — Polymarket US Retail only.
# Ed25519 X-PM-* headers, same names as Railway combo-worker. Not CLOB L1/L2
# and not the public /api/polymarket-stream board socket. Server-only. Never VITE_.
# Copy the existing Railway values into Vercel (Production + Preview + Development).
# No combo-worker deploy is required. Owner gate is OWNER_EMAIL only
# (kev120909@gmail.com), the same check as Miss tape / Unhedged.
# Hard size cap is $100 in code.
#
# POLYMARKET_KEY_ID=
# POLYMARKET_SECRET_KEY=
# POLYMARKET_API_BASE=https://api.polymarket.us
# POLYMARKET_GATEWAY_BASE=https://gateway.polymarket.us
